You are a robotics test analyst. You are given EVIDENCE computed by code from simulated pick-and-place runs of a fixed controller. Explain WHY it fails as a few testable hypotheses. Rules: (1) cite evidence ids (like E7) in evidence_refs for every claim; use only ids that appear below. (2) Do NOT state statistics or counts in your own words: refer to evidence by id, because a person will see the numbers from the evidence table, not from you. (3) region is a machine-checkable predicate: scenario axes with [lo, hi] inside the allowed bounds. (4) levers may only be these tunable parameters: grip_force, grasp_hold_steps, retry_count, lift_speed, lift_height. (5) prediction must be testable, for example which failures should disappear if a lever moves. Return between 1 and 4 hypotheses with ids H1, H2, ... You do not decide pass or fail.

Reply with a single JSON object matching this JSON Schema, and nothing else:
{"$defs": {"Hypothesis": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"id": {"title": "Id", "type": "string"}, "statement": {"minLength": 1, "title": "Statement", "type": "string"}, "region": {"additionalProperties": {"items": {"type": "number"}, "type": "array"}, "title": "Region", "type": "object"}, "mechanism": {"minLength": 1, "title": "Mechanism", "type": "string"}, "levers": {"items": {"$ref": "#/$defs/Lever"}, "minItems": 1, "title": "Levers", "type": "array"}, "prediction": {"minLength": 1, "title": "Prediction", "type": "string"}, "evidence_refs": {"items": {"type": "string"}, "minItems": 1, "title": "Evidence Refs", "type": "array"}}, "required": ["id", "statement", "region", "mechanism", "levers", "prediction", "evidence_refs"], "title": "Hypothesis", "type": "object"}, "Lever": {"additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"param": {"title": "Param", "type": "string"}, "direction": {"enum": ["increase", "decrease"], "title": "Direction", "type": "string"}}, "required": ["param", "direction"], "title": "Lever", "type": "object"}}, "additionalProperties": false, "properties": {"hypotheses": {"items": {"$ref": "#/$defs/Hypothesis"}, "maxItems": 5, "minItems": 1, "title": "Hypotheses", "type": "array"}}, "required": ["hypotheses"], "title": "HypothesisList", "type": "object"}

reply:
{
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "id": "H1",
      "statement": "Insufficient grip force for heavy cubes with low friction causes MISSED_GRASP because the friction force cannot overcome the cube's weight during lift.",
      "region": {
        "mass_kg": [0.69, 1.0],
        "friction": [0.1, 0.23]
      },
      "mechanism": "The maximum friction force (grip_force * friction) is less than the gravitational force (mass_kg * 9.81), so the cube never leaves the table or slips immediately.",
      "levers": [
        {
          "param": "grip_force",
          "direction": "increase"
        }
      ],
      "prediction": "Increasing grip_force will eliminate MISSED_GRASP failures in the high-mass, low-friction region.",
      "evidence_refs": ["E46", "E39", "E2"]
    },
    {
      "id": "H2",
      "statement": "Small cube size combined with low friction reduces contact area and friction force, leading to MISSED_GRASP.",
      "region": {
        "size_m": [0.03, 0.047],
        "friction": [0.1, 0.47]
      },
      "mechanism": "Small cubes have smaller contact patches, requiring higher normal force to generate sufficient friction; current grip_force is too low for the low-friction, small-size combination.",
      "levers": [
        {
          "param": "grip_force",
          "direction": "increase"
        }
      ],
      "prediction": "Increasing grip_force will reduce MISSED_GRASP failures in the small-size, low-friction region.",
      "evidence_refs": ["E38", "E13", "E8"]
    },
    {
      "id": "H3",
      "statement": "High sensor noise causes misperception of cube pose, leading to MISSED_GRASP and PLACED_OUTSIDE_ZONE, exacerbated by zero retries.",
      "region": {
        "sensor_noise_m": [0.024, 0.03]
      },
      "mechanism": "Noisy perception causes the gripper to miss the cube or misplace it; with retry_count=0, there is no opportunity to re-perceive and correct.",
      "levers": [
        {
          "param": "retry_count",
          "direction": "increase"
        }
      ],
      "prediction": "Setting retry_count > 0 will reduce failures in high sensor noise regions.",
      "evidence_refs": ["E32", "E41", "E43", "E45"]
    },
    {
      "id": "H4",
      "statement": "High gripper delay combined with small cube size causes MISSED_GRASP because the fingers have insufficient time to conform before lift.",
      "region": {
        "size_m": [0.03, 0.047],
        "gripper_delay_steps": [13, 20]
      },
      "mechanism": "The gripper_delay_steps postpones the close command; with small cubes, the fingers need more time to close fully. The current grasp_hold_steps (10) may be too short after the delayed close command.",
      "levers": [
        {
          "param": "grasp_hold_steps",
          "direction": "increase"
        }
      ],
      "prediction": "Increasing grasp_hold_steps will reduce MISSED_GRASP failures in the high-delay, small-size region.",
      "evidence_refs": ["E40", "E37", "E38"]
    }
  ]
}

